======================================================================================================================
L57 -- the nonlocal functional: the one successor L56's theorem does not cover
======================================================================================================================
    a0 footings: canonical 9.3619e-11 m/s^2, alt 1.1279e-10 m/s^2
    convention: ds^2 = -(1+2 Phi) dt^2 + (1-2 Psi) dx^2;  slip s = Phi - Psi;  lensing potential
    (Phi+Psi)/2.  A slip is observable only through its GRADIENT: a constant s shifts Phi and Psi
    by equal and opposite constants and moves neither dynamics nor lensing.  That fact is what
    makes this lane's crux a gradient ratio and not an overlap.
    cosmic mean baryon density (Planck h, Omega_b = 0.049): 4.181e-28 kg/m^3

